AB  - A 35-year-old woman had a liver spleen scan for vague abdominal pain without a history of abdominal trauma. Liver-spleen imaging failed to reveal a normal spleen in the splenic fossa but did show a small splenule. A large incidental hot focus in the pelvis overlying the bladder region was shown to be the spleen, not the bladder, by additional renal and bladder imaging. The authors report an unusual case of pelvic spleen and splenule on Tc-99m phytate images verified with Tc-99m DMSA images to exclude a supranumerary pelvic kidney.
