AU  - Bittar, I
AU  - Cohen Solal, J L
AU  - Cabanis, P
PY  - 2001
T2  - Presse medicale (Paris, France : 1983)
VL  - 30
IS  - 20
SP  - 1005
EP  - 6
AB  - BACKGROUND: Volvulus of the mobile spleen is a rare condition generally manifested by acute sudden onset abdominal pain localized in the left flank. Ultrasound or computed tomographic imaging generally provides the diagnosis. CASE REPORT: An 18-year-old patient was hospitalized for acute pain of the left flank that had begun 48 hours earlier. The abdominal scan visualized a volvulus of a mobile spleen. Laparoscopic distortion was successful, allowing normal recoloration of the spleen. DISCUSSION: Rapid intervention is crucial for conservative treatment. Laparoscopic treatment allows distortion manoeuvres and splenopexia using a mesh. This is the first reported case of successful conservative laparoscopic treatment of volvulus of a mobile spleen.
