TI  - Diagnosis of splenic torsion: a combined radiographic approach
AU  - Dublin, A.B.
AU  - Rosenquist, C.J.
PY  - 1976
T2  - British Journal of Radiology
VL  - 49
IS  - 588
SP  - 1045
EP  - 1046
DO  - 10.1259/0007-1285-49-588-1045
AB  - Torsion of the spleen about its pedicle is a rare condition in North America and Europe, comprising only 0.2% of splenectomies performed at the Mayo Clinic between 1904 and 1945 (Pugh, 1946). In underdeveloped nations the rate of occurrence is probably slightly higher due to the increased presence of splenomegaly secondary to malnutrition and malaria. Although this event is seldom suspected preoperatively, a thorough radiographic evaluation may be useful. This report describes an approach to the correct diagnosis employing barium studies, diagnostic ultrasound, nuclear medicine and angiography. By utilizing all of these procedures, a specific diagnosis may be possible.
