EP  - 337
DO  - 10.1016/0002-9610(74)90044-0
AB  - A case is presented of a five year old girl in whom an acute surgical abdomen developed due to torsion and infarction of an accessory spleen. Other similar cases in the literature are reviewed. The incidence, location, and embryologic aspects of accessory spleens are discussed. Infarction of an accessory spleen, although rarely the cause of an acute surgical abdomen, should be considered in the differential diagnosis. © 1974.
