TI  - Torsion of the spleen: a case report
AU  - DeBartolo Jr, H.M.
AU  - Van Heerden, J.A.
AU  - Lynn, H.B.
AU  - Norris, D.G.
PY  - 1973
T2  - Mayo Clinic Proceedings
VL  - 48
IS  - 11
SP  - 783
EP  - 786
AB  - Torsion of the spleen presented as an abdominal emergency in a 4 yr old boy. The diagnosis was suspected by visualization of a retroperitoneal mass on an abdominal roentgenogram, intravenous pyelogram, and barium enema, and by the appearance of thrombocytosis and Howell Jolly bodies in a peripheral blood smear. Removal of an infarcted spleen was followed by recovery; no antibiotics were used. This case illustrates some of the diagnostic and therapeutic considerations pertaining to torsion of the spleen. Proper surgical treatment is particularly important; the correct treatment is splenectomy.
