AB  - A case of a newborn with a Erythroblastosis fetalis and “obstructive” type jaundice with an abdominal tumor, is presented. As the jaundice was found to be elicited by Rh incompatibility, the absence of a palpable spleen at the normal site suggested the possibility of the abdominal mass being an ectopic spleen. This diagnosis was confirmed at operation. The possibility of a preexisting developmental defect is elaborated upon. Copyright © 1971, Wiley Blackwell. All rights reserved
