DO  - 10.1159/000306852
AB  - Report on a 25-year-old patient whose anamnesis shows several indefiniteabdominal affections after injury in early childhood. A dystopic spleen is found instead of a suspected uterine tumour. This is situated in the large omentum and was adherent to the lateral part of the right chorda utero-inguinalis. The causes of abnormal position of the spleen and deformities of this organ are discussed, and similar cases are quoted. © 1957 S. Karger AG, Basel.
