AB  - The basic pathogenesis of ptosis due to spleen Qi deficiency involves inadequate spleen Qi, muscle and tendon malnourishment, and weakness of the eyelid muscles. In this study, we used the time-based meridian Nazhi method to select acupoints along spleen and stomach meridians for acupuncture, in combination with conventional acupuncture at periorbital acupoints, to treat ptosis caused by spleen Qi deficiency. This approach aims to strengthen spleen and stomach, tonify Qi and blood, regulate meridians, raise clear Yang, and lift sagging tissues. Clinical cases are presented to demonstrate the significant efficacy of this treatment. The time-based meridian Nazhi method is one of the acupuncture point selection techniques in the meridian Nazhi method, and when combined with conventional acupoint puncture, it offers a new approach and method for treating ptosis due to spleen Qi deficiency and other related patterns. © 2025 Editorial department of China Jounal of Chinese Ophthalmology. All rights reserved.
