AB  - We describe the case of a wandering spleen presenting as a lower abdominal mass causing acute abdomen with respiratory discomfort. On ultrasonography and computed tomography, mass was an enlarged ectopic spleen with infarction of splenic vessels and left-sided diaphragmatic hernia. On exploratory laparotomy, ectopic pelvic spleen with 2 1/2 turns in the splenic pedicle was found. Although accessory spleen is found in 10% to 30% of population, a wandering twisted pelvic spleen presenting as a gynecologic emergency is extremely rare. © 2007 Lippincott Williams & Wilkins, Inc.
