AB  - Splenosis is the ectopic implantation (autotransplantation) of splenic tissue usually after splenectomy performed because of trauma or hematologic disorders. A 20-year-old man with no symptoms who underwent splenectomy 10 years earlier after a traumatic rupture of the spleen was referred to the authors' department to identify any residual splenic tissue. Tc-99m sulfur colloid liver-spleen scintigraphy showed multifocal accumulation of the radiopharmaceutical as a result of splenosis in the left side of the abdomen mimicking massive gastrointestinal bleeding.
