AB  - We present an unusual case of gastric volvulus associated with congenital diaphragmatic hernia, wandering spleen, and intrathoracic kidney diagnosed on imaging and managed surgically. Our patient presented late to our hospital (2 days duration of severe symptoms), so inspite of correct diagnosis and immediate surgery the patient needed total gastrectomy due to gangrenous stomach. So, we emphasize prompt radiological diagnosis and immediate surgery to avoid gastric and splenic necrosis. Radiological findings and the appearance of this complex congenital malformation is reported.
