AB  - We report a case of a torsion of wandering spleen with portal vein thrombosis. A 34-year-woman was admitted to our hospital with abdominal pain. Contrast-enhanced CT depicted the unenhanced ectopic spleen, which did not showed contrast enhancement. Twisted vessels were detected at the hilum of the spleen. Portal thrombosis was detected. Splenectomy was performed and yield the diagnosis of the infarction of torsed spleen and venous thrombosis in gastroepiploic vein.
