AB  - Torsioned wandering spleen should be considered in patients who have an intrapelvic mass with acute abdominal symptoms. Although, color Doppler US, CT and angiography are highly accurate for indicating the correct diagnosis in such patients, a combined US and laparoscopy is cost effective and enables the surgeon not only to confirm the diagnosis but also perform either splenopexy or splenectomy depending on the vascular status of the spleen.
