AB  - In our institute, we have treated 249 cases of rectal cancer in the period 1967-1978. Recently, we have achieved good results by two new methods: (1) Since 1976, we have been using an improved suture device for the low anterior resection. Generally, it is difficult to secure anastomosis at the portion of the dentate line, but using this method, we have performed 20 cases of low anterior resection easily and accurately. (2) We have devised a new method of chemotherapy against liver metastasis of colorectal cancer. This method consists of chemotherapy via the portal vein through splenopexy - percutaneous transplenic injection of anticancer drugs. We have performed this method on 13 cases, and obtained good results.
